stdout | tests/bidcost.test.ts > O: can the BID COST function fix these problems at all? (structural analysis) > O3: is congestionCost even meaningful, or is it double-counting occupancy?
O3 robot AMR-01 at 1,0 -> pickup 3,9: distance=13 congestionCost=2.0
O3 CONGESTION_WEIGHT=1, and computeCongestion gives an OCCUPIED cell weight 3 and each neighbour 1.
O3 So merely passing through a cell with ONE robot on it costs 3 — the same as 3 extra steps of travel.
O3 And since every robot sees the same congestion field, congestionCost is IDENTICAL across robots
O3 for the same task at the same tick — it shifts all bids by a constant and cannot change the winner
O3 UNLESS robots are at different distances. Check spread:
