O3 travelCost      across bidders: min=17 max=36 distinct=11

stdout | tests/bidcost.test.ts > O: can the BID COST function fix these problems at all? (structural analysis) > O4: does the bid cost know anything about the OTHER robots' plans?
O4 calculateBid(robot, task, world) reads: robot.position/battery/path/model, task.pickup/dropoff/weight/priority/deadline, world.map.congestion, world.tick.
O4 It does NOT read: any other robot's currentTaskId, path, or status.
O4 => two robots bidding for the SAME task cannot see that they would route through the same corridor.
O4 AMR-01 path and AMR-05 path share 1 cells: 3,9
O4 => contention is invisible to the auction. It is only discovered later, by PIBT, as a conflict.

stdout | tests/bidcost.test.ts > O: can the BID COST function fix these problems at all? (structural analysis) > O5: the assignment is greedy-per-task with no global load balance
