stdout | tests/survey.test.ts > M: the all-below-floor starvation > M3: battery floor vs charging threshold — are they even consistent?
M3 constants:
M3   MIN_BATTERY_TO_BID_PERCENT = 20  (isEligible hard gate in assign.ts)
M3   BATTERY_SAFETY_RESERVE_PERCENT = 15  (cost.ts infeasibleReason 'battery')
M3   RECHARGE_TARGET_PERCENT = 50  (leave charging here)
M3   BATTERY_PERCENT_PER_CELL = 0.5, CHARGE_PERCENT_PER_TICK = 2
M3 => a robot that finishes charging leaves at 50%. It can then accept a task costing up to
M3    (50-15)/0.5 = 70 cells. Fine. But a robot at 20% can only afford (20-15)/0.5 = 10 cells,
M3    and a robot at 20% that loses its task and idles has 0 incentive to charge until 19%.
M3    The gap between 'can still bid' (>=20) and 'wants to charge' (needsToCharge) is the hazard zone.

